1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,420
Here's a fun sound...

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,100
Ch!

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,460
Ch!

4
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,880
Ch!

5
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,420
This sound has two spellings!

6
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:12,740
We can write ch, or we can write tch.

7
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,780
You hear it in chair, and you hear it in catch.

8
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,500
Same sound, different spelling.

9
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,240
So which one do we write?

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,920
We look at the vowel right before it.

11
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:28,760
Here is the rule.

12
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:33,260
Right after one short vowel, we write tch.

13
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:34,700
Listen.

14
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:37,980
C - a - tch.

15
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:39,260
Catch!

16
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:44,140
That a is a short vowel, so we write tch.

17
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:46,310
Here are more.

18
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:48,240
Match.

19
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:50,020
Watch.

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:52,000
Fetch.

21
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:56,140
Most of the time, we just write ch.

22
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,900
At the start of a word, nothing comes before it.

23
00:00:59,960 --> 00:00:59,960
Chair.

24
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:03,160
Chin.

25
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:11,180
After another consonant, like the n in lunch.

26
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:12,220
Bench.

27
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:16,660
After a long vowel, which says its own name.

28
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:18,240
Beach.

29
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:19,900
Coach.

30
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,140
All three take ch.

31
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,160
But watch out!

32
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:28,120
A few little words break this rule.

33
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,040
Much, such, rich and which.

34
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,380
They have short vowels, but they still use ch.

35
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,920
These are special words, so try to remember them!

36
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,260
You will meet longer ones too.

37
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:48,100
Ostrich.

38
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,080
Attach.

39
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,510
Now, it is your turn!

40
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,300
Here is the word.

41
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:55,420
Coach.

42
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:59,600
Do we write it with ch, or with tch?

43
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,400
It is ch!

44
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:06,030
Because o and a make a long vowel.

45
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,320
So let's remember it together.

46
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,020
After a short vowel we write tch.

47
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:15,700
Everywhere else we write just ch.

48
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,460
And don't forget those special words!

49
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:22,760
Every spelling rule is waiting in the English Learning app.

50
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,700
Download it today.

51
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,680
It won't cost you a thing!
